# .leakscanignore — repo-root whole-file exemptions for scripts/leak_scan.py
#
# This file is discovered by `leak_scan.py --staged` (whose scan root is the repo
# top) and by any `--root .` scan. It exempts ONLY the secret-scanner's own
# TEST + FIXTURE files, which contain FAKE secrets BY DESIGN (synthetic AWS /
# RSA / Slack / Braintrust tokens, split-secret reassembly cases, a fake
# incident report). Self-scanning that corpus would self-flag the intentional
# fixtures — a bootstrapping false positive, not a real leak.
# DO NOT add production code or any SUT (protocol-sift/) config here. Production
# pattern-constant false positives are handled with narrow inline
# "# leak-scan: allow <check.id>" comments on the specific line instead, so the
# rest of the file stays fully scanned.
# Syntax: one glob per line, relative to repo root. '#' starts a comment.

# The scanner's own unit-test suite (asserts on fake secrets it must detect).
scripts/test_leak_scan.py
# The scanner's red-team corpus: block_* are SUPPOSED to contain fake secrets;
# ok_* are negative cases. run_redteam.sh drives these as fixtures.
scripts/redteam/**
# The drift-check unit test embeds SYNTHETIC verdict-vocabulary tokens
# (MALICE / NON_MALICE / INCONCLUSIVE / SUSPICIOUS) and fake YAML by design;
# the scanner mis-reads those test strings as secret assignments. It is a
# TEST file (like scripts/test_leak_scan.py), so whole-file exempt it.
eval/diagnosis/test_contract_scorer_drift.py
# Diagnosis Protocol synthetic test fixtures (eval/diagnosis/): synthetic
# round-score JSONs, fake labeled judge sets, and synthetic IOC values BY
# DESIGN. They carry no real secrets/keys/ground-truth. Mirrors the existing
# scripts/redteam/** + test_leak_scan.py fixture exemptions.
eval/diagnosis/fixtures/**
